From uab8277113f65c05e at groups.google.com  Tue Jan 23 23:04:53 2018
From: uab8277113f65c05e at groups.google.com (Altuna Akalin)
Date: Tue, 23 Jan 2018 23:04:53 +0000
Subject: Re: [methylkit_discussion] Problem with DMR analysis in MethylKit
Message-ID: <pz_1lCDn090.1RUQPl4vBAAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <pz_1lCDn090.DKiYLvcWBAAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
References: <pz_1lCDn090.ux4-7Kc0AgAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com> <pz_1lCDn090.DKiYLvcWBAAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/methylkit_discussion/c/pz_1lCDn090/m/1RUQPl4vBAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

meth <- unite(myobj, destrand=FALSE)
after this step you get an object with no CpGs in it. your individual samples comes from different chromosomes and they can not be merged. unite() merges the samples to a single table based on the coordinates of CpGs or regions. Please read the docs, this should be clear enough there.

Best,
Altuna

