Hi

I have used :
meth.min=unite(myobj,min.per.group=1L)

but the problem still exist for me, and also it decrease the number of record in "meth" object.

So, I have tried to replace NA  to Zero,  so all of NAs now are 0s but I could not get successful run on the below commands:

getCorrelation(meth,plot=TRUE)
clusterSamples(meth, dist="correlation", method="ward", plot=TRUE)

myDiff2=calculateDiffMeth(meth2)

 I have got same error when I changed NA to zero or when I used "min.group=1L".

Dear friends is there any method to check the problems of .COV data to make it runnable for methylKit.

I mean we could normalize or remove some rows in expression array, is there any function to find out what's the problem exactly?

thanks,
Ahmad

On Wed, Jan 24, 2018 at 2:34 AM, Altuna Akalin <aak...@gmail.com> wrote:

> meth <- unite(myobj, destrand=FALSE)
> after this step you get an object with no CpGs in it. your individual samples comes from different chromosomes and they can not be merged. unite() merges the samples to a single table based on the coordinates of CpGs or regions. Please read the docs, this should be clear enough there.
>
> Best,
> Altuna

